      "title": "Use the z-score formula for a sample mean",
      "lines": [
       {
        "text": "For a sample of 100 the standard error is $\\dfrac{12}{\\sqrt{100}} = 1.2$."
       },
       {
        "tex": "-2.26 &= \\frac{\\bar{x} - 87.3}{12/\\sqrt{100}}"
       },
       {
        "tex": "-2.26 &= \\frac{\\bar{x} - 87.3}{1.2}"
       },
       {
        "tex": "\\bar{x} - 87.3 &= -2.712"
       },
       {
        "tex": "\\bar{x} &= 84.588"
       },
       {
        "tex": "&\\approx 84.6"
       }
      ]
     }
